The '''TIE/sf space superiority fighter''', also known as the '''First Order SF TIE Fighter''' or '''Special Forces TIE fighter''', was a [[starfighter]] model used by the [[First Order]], a specialized version of the [[TIE/fo space superiority fighter]]. It was a two-seater unlike the previous [[TIE series|TIE models]] and was outfitted with enhanced weapons and sensor systems as well as a [[hyperdrive]] and [[deflector shield]]s. The TIE/sf was reserved for members of the First Order's elite [[First Order Special Forces|Special Forces]].

==Characteristics==
{{Quote|Use the toggle on the left to switch between missiles, cannons, and mag pulse&mdash;use the sight on the right to aim, triggers to fire!''"<br />"''This is very complicated.|Poe Dameron and FN-2187 shortly before their escape from the ''[[Finalizer]]''|<ref name="TFA" />}}
[[File:Sf_space_superiority_fighter_cross-section.jpg|thumb|left|200px|Cross-sections of a TIE/sf space superiority fighter]]
A two-seat strike fighter used by the First Order's elite Special Forces [[pilot]]s, the TIE/sf boasted weapons far more powerful than a standard TIE, combining [[laser cannon]]s with a heavy weapons [[turret]] and a [[mag-pulse warhead]] launcher,<ref name="Cross" /> giving the fighter the ability to deliver special ordnance. Although the pilot had the ability to fire all weapons, the turret was ideally controlled by the rear-facing gunner.

Special Forces TIEs were equipped with [[hyperdrive]]s to enable the fighter to go on long-range missions far from a base or carrier ship, enhanced deflector shields, and high-yield cells that provided additional power to onboard systems, which were necessary because of its more powerful weapons and stronger shields.<ref name="Cross" /> These versatile attack ships were used for both reconnaissance and combat operations.<ref name="TFA" />

This variant of the TIE fighter could be visually distinguished from its regular counterpart by the laser turret below the cockpit and the red flashes on its left side; similarly, the Special Forces pilots who operated them also had red flashes on their helmets, in a callback to the flight barons of the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="TFA" />

==History==
[[File:TFA-TIE-take-off.png|thumb|left|220px|Poe and Finn's TIE/sf attempts to escape the hangar and reach Jakku.]]
The captured [[Resistance]] ace pilot [[Poe Dameron]] alongside a then-recently-defected stormtrooper identified as [[Finn|FN-2187]] hijacked a [[Unidentified TIE/sf space superiority fighter (Finalizer)|TIE/sf space superiority fighter]] from [[Hangar Six]] to [[Escape from the Finalizer|escape]] from the [[Resurgent-class Star Destroyer|''Resurgent''-class Star Destroyer]] ''[[Finalizer]]''. The two initially ran into a problem due to the TIE still being connected to the ship by a supply cable. They finally broke free, and escaped the Star Destroyer, only to be shot by missiles fired from the ship's ventral cannon. The fighter ended up crashing on [[Jakku]], although both Poe and FN-2187 survived.<ref name="TFA" />

Numerous TIE/sf's later took part in the [[Battle of Takodana]], assisting in leveling the [[Takodana Castle]] and killing many of its inhabitants, and engaged Resistance [[T-70 X-wing starfighter]]s in combat above the ruins. Although the TIE fighters were successful in attacking the castle and supporting infantry, they proved to be no match to Resistance fighter forces, ending up losing many TIEs against the versatility of X-wings and Poe Dameron's superb skills, forcing the First Order to retreat.<ref name="TFA" />

After the [[Battle of Kestro City|Battle of Kestro]], [[Iden Versio]], [[Shriv Suurgav]], [[Zay Versio]], and [[Dio]] stole two Special Forces TIEs to sneak aboard [[Commander]] [[Gideon Hask]]'s Star Destroyer the ''[[Retribution]]''.<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref>

[[File:EscapingStarkillerBase-CaptainPhasma1.png|thumb|right|250px|Captain Phasma and TN-3465 were aboard a TIE/sf when Starkiller was destroyed.]]
Some Special Forces TIEs were part of the [[Starkiller aerial defense force]] during the [[Battle of Starkiller Base]]; however, they were unable to stop Poe Dameron from destroying the key [[thermal oscillator]] which led to a chain reaction, destroying the [[planet]].<ref name="TFA" />

Zay and Shriv used a Special Forces TIE to escape the ''Retribution'' and head to [[D'Qar]] to deliver the [[Project Resurrection]] and [[Mandator IV-class Siege Dreadnought|''Mandator IV''-class Siege Dreadnought]] information to the Resistance and go to [[Outer Rim Territories]] to find allies for them.<ref name="Battlefront II" />

[[Captain]] [[Phasma]] and [[TN-3465]] used a TIE/sf to travel to [[Luprora]] to hunt down and assassinate [[Sol Rivas]], who also used a Special Forces TIE.<ref name="Captain Phasma 2">[[Captain Phasma 2|''Captain Phasma'' 2]]</ref>

During the [[Battle of D'Qar|Evacuation of D'Qar]], some Special Forces TIEs chased and attempted to shoot down Poe Dameron's X-wing ''[[Black One]]'' while he was destroying the ''[[Fulminatrix]]''{{'s}} turrets, and some Special Forces TIEs tried destroying their entire fleet of [[MG-100 StarFortress SF-17 heavy bomber|MG-100 StarFortress SF-17]] strategic [[bomber]]s before they could destroy the dreadnought.<ref name="TLJ" />

[[File:TIE_Silencer_in_Action.png|thumb|left|250px|Kylo Ren's fighter escort fires on the ''Raddus''{{'}} bridge.]]
Later, during the First Order's [[Battle of Oetchi]], [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]] personally attacked the Resistance's flagship, ''[[Raddus]]'', in his [[TIE/vn space superiority fighter|TIE Silencer]] with three Special Forces TIEs flanking him. When Ren, sensing the presence of his mother, [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa Solo]], hesitated to fire on the ''Raddus'' bridge, his wingmen destroyed it instead, using missiles, killing everyone on the bridge except for Organa, who was incapacitated in the attack. All three Special Forces TIEs were destroyed soon after, forcing Ren to retreat.<ref name="TLJ" />

Several TIE/sf's were present at the [[Battle of Crait]] and pursued the ''Millennium Falcon'' through the planet's interior during the battle.<ref name="TLJ" />

More TIE/sfs were later present during the [[Assault on Naboo (First Order)|assault of Naboo]].<ref name="Legacy of Vader 5">{{WebCite|url=https://aiptcomics.com/2025/06/20/marvel-preview-star-wars-legacy-of-vader-5|text=Marvel Preview: Star Wars: Legacy of Vader #5|archivedate=20250620192913}}</ref>

In [[35 ABY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' dates the events of ''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'' to one [[Standard year|year]] after the [[Hosnian Cataclysm|Starkiller Incident]], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[34 ABY]]. Therefore, the events of ''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'' must take place in [[35 ABY]].</ref> several squadrons of Special Forces TIE fighters and [[TIE/wi Interceptor|TIE whisper starfighters]] arrived at the [[Sinta Glacier Colony]], preparing to destroy the ''Falcon''. TIEs pursued the ''Falcon'' through the Glacier and a number of [[star system]]s while [[Hyperspace skipping|lightspeed skipping]].<ref name="Episode IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
During the early days of brainstorming for [[Star Wars: Episode VII The Force Awakens|''Star Wars'': Episode VII ''The Force Awakens'']], concept artist [[Doug Chiang]] suggested including TIE fighters with headlights, as he thought that it was very cool when the ''Millennium Falcon'' showed its headlights in [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']].<ref name="Instagram">{{Instagram|username=doug_chiang|url=p/BqxNa51Fbug|name=[[Doug Chiang]]|quote=In our early days of brainstorming for EP7, I thought it would be fun to see headlights on the TIE Fighters. I always thought it was cool that the Millennium Falcon had headlights when it went into the asteroid cave in EP5. #starwars #fun #scifi|archiveurl=https://archive.is/bMvZk}}</ref>

